ection 3\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nManufacturer: APX\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\",\"annotations\":null,\"meta\":null}", "type": "function_call_output"}','2025-09-27 01:56:50');
INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(30,'a7195a06-0d55-4035-af14-5a1cd28c6294','{"id": "msg_68d744631c4481969f12fb5737d9ee4506dab987d467974e", "content": [{"annotations": [], "text": "**Direct Answer**: Yes, regular Tylenol (acetaminophen) is covered for seniors under the Ontario Drug Benefit (ODB) program.\n\n### Coverage Details\n- **Generic Name**: Acetaminophen\n- **DIN**: 02230434 (example: ACET 120)\n- **Coverage**: It is covered without Limited Use criteria.\n\n### Billing Information\n- **Strength**: 120 mg (other strengths available are 325 mg and 500 mg)\n- **Therapeutic Class**: Central Nervous System Drugs\n- **Category**: Analgesics Miscellaneous Analgesics and Antipyretics\n- It does not require prior authorization for coverage.\n\n### Alternatives\nOther available formulations include:\n- **Apo-Acetaminophen Caplets**:\n  - DIN 02229977: 500 mg\n  - DIN 02229873: 325 mg\n\nThese alternatives may have different pricing and coverage details.\n\n### Next Steps\nEnsure the patient is enrolled in the ODB program to take advantage of the medication coverage. Further information and specifics for the drug can be reviewed on the [Ontario Drug Benefit Formulary](https://www.formulary.health.gov.on.ca/formulary/results.xhtml?q=02230434).", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message"}','2025-09-27 01:56:55');
