\nPrice: $0.1811 per unit\\\\nDaily Cost: $N/A\\\\nCoverage: General Benefit\\\\nSection 3 Section 12\\\\nChronic Use\\\\n\\\\nManufacturer: AUR\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\",\"annotations\":null,\"meta\":null}", "type": "function_call_output"}','2025-09-29 01:21:20');
INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(68,'dae5390d-ca86-4d64-b748-72d4f8c79bdc','{"id": "msg_68d9df1129c08194bdd6e8d49d630de60ae8a1049ffe85ea", "content": [{"annotations": [], "text": "**Direct Answer**: Yes, Ozempic (semaglutide) is covered by the Ontario Drug Benefit (ODB).\n\n**Coverage Details**:\n- **DIN**: 02540258\n- **Strength**: 0.68 mg/mL\n- **Coverage Type**: General Benefit\n- Ozempic is primarily indicated for the management of type 2 diabetes, but it may also be utilized for weight management in certain patients as per specific clinical guidelines. \n\n**Billing Information**:\n- **Price**: Approximately $223.26 per unit.\n\n**Alternatives**:\nWhile Ozempic is covered, it is primarily used for diabetes management. If a patient is looking for weight loss options outside of diabetes treatment, alternative medications or therapies may need to be considered.\n\n**Next Steps**:\nFor prescribing, ensure that the indication aligns with ODB coverage criteria, and document the patient''s clinical need adequately. You can refer to the official formulary for more information: [ODB Formulary - Ozempic](https://www.formulary.health.gov.on.ca/formulary/results.xhtml?q=02540258).\n\nAlways check for the most current policies and eligibility requirements when prescribing.", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message"}','2025-09-29 01:21:24');
INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(69,'53711fac-37d0-47c2-8922-2d6846963d1b','{"content": "Can my patient get ADP funding for a CPAP machine?", "role": "user"}','2025-09-29 01:21:51');
INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(70,'53711fac-37d0-47c2-8922-2d6846963d1b','{"arguments": "{\"query\":\"Can my patient get funding for a CPAP machine?\"}", "call_id": "call_fu2tQN6BVrdEdrF8yMO1S3ME", "name": "adp_get", "type": "function_call", "id": "fc_68d9df305f54819689d336e044c137c102e7edb03d694e44", "status": "completed"}','2025-09-29 01:21:56');
INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(71,'53711fac-37d0-47c2-8922-2d6846963d1b','{"call_id": "call_fu2tQN6BVrdEdrF8yMO1S3ME", "output": "{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"provenance\\\": [\\n    \\\"sql\\\",\\n    \\\"vector\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.99,\\n  \\\"answer\\\": \\\"Yes, your patient can receive funding for a CPAP machine through ADP in Ontario. ADP covers 75% of the cost, and the patient is responsible for the remaining 25%. Low-income patients may be eligible for the Chronic Equipment Pool (CEP) which can eliminate their 25% share. A valid prescription from an authorized prescriber is required for funding approval.\\\",\\n  \\\"answer_confidence\\\": 0.8,\\n  \\\"eligibility\\\": null,\\n  \\\"exclusions\\\": [],\\n  \\\"funding\\\": {\\n    \\\"client_share_percent\\\": 25.0,\\n    \\\"adp_contribution\\\": 75.0,\\n    \\\"max_contribution\\\": null,\\n    \\\"repair_coverage\\\": \\\"Not covered\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"cep\\\": null,\\n  \\\"citations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"ADP Respiratory Equipment Manual\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"adp:respiratory:335, page 22\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": 22,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://files.ontario.ca/moh-adp-policy-and-administration-manual-respiratory-equipment-2024-11-08.pdf\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"ADP Core Policies and Procedures Manual\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"adp:core_manual:335, page 22\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": 22,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://files.ontario.ca/moh-adp-policies-and-procedures-manual-assistive-devices-program-2023-07-01.pdf\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"ADP Respiratory Equipment Manual\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"adp:respiratory:300.01, page 20\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": 20,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://files.ontario.ca/moh-adp-policy-and-administration-manual-respiratory-equipment-2024-11-08.pdf\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"ADP Core Policies and Procedures Manual\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"adp:core_manual:300.01, page 20\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": 20,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://files.ontario.ca/moh-adp-policies-and-procedures-manual-assistive-devices-program-2023-07-01.pdf\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"ADP Core Policies and Procedures Manual\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"adp:core_manual:325, page 22\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": 22,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://files.ontario.ca/moh-adp-policies-and-procedures-manual-assistive-devices-program-2023-07-01.pdf\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"ADP Respiratory Equipment Manual\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"adp:respiratory:325, page 22\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": 22,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://files.ontario.ca/moh-adp-policy-and-administration-manual-respiratory-equipment-2024-11-08.pdf\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"ADP Core Policies and Procedures Manual\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"adp:core_manual:315.02, page 22\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": 22,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://files.ontario.ca/moh-adp-policies-and-procedures-manual-assistive-devices-program-2023-07-01.pdf\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"ADP Respiratory Equipment Manual\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"adp:respiratory:315.02, page 22\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": 22,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://files.ontario.ca/moh-adp-policy-and-administration-manual-respiratory-equipment-2024-11-08.pdf\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"conflicts\\\": [],\\n  \\\"context\\\": \\\"**ADP Policy Context:**\\\\n\u2022 adp:respiratory:335 - Medical Eligibility Criteria for Positive...: Airway Pressure Systems\\\\n(CPAP/APAP/BPAP)\\\\nThe ADP provides funding for positive airway pressure systems for\\\\nindividuals with a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea syndrome (OSAS)\\\\nand the presence of s...\\\\n\u2022 adp:core_manual:335 - Medical Eligibility Criteria for Positive...: Airway Pressure Systems\\\\n(CPAP/APAP/BPAP)\\\\nThe ADP provides funding for positive airway pressure systems for\\\\nindividuals with a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea syndrome (OSAS)\\\\nand the presence of s...\\\\n\u2022 adp:respiratory:300.01 - The ADP will provide funding assistance to eligible applican...: following respiratory Devices, when prescribed by a Physician or Nurse\\\\nPractitioner.\\\\n\u2022 apnea/cardiorespiratory monitors\\\\n\u2022 medication compressors\\\\n\u2022 high output air compressors\\\\n\u2022 airway clearance device...\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"\ud83d\udccb Device: cpap machine (Respiratory Equipment) | \u2705 ELIGIBLE for funding: ADP covers 75.0%, patient pays 25.0%\\\",\\n  \\\"interpretation_notes\\\": {\\n    \\\"null_values\\\": \\\"null means ''not determined from query'' - may require follow-up\\\",\\n    \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"0.99 - High confidence\\\",\\n    \\\"cep\\\": \\\"Chronic Equipment Pool eliminates patient cost for low-income patients\\\"\\n  }\\n}\",\"annotations\":null,\"meta\":null}", "type": "function_call_output"}','2025-09-29 01:21:56');
INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(72,'53711fac-37d0-47c2-8922-2d6846963d1b','{"id": "msg_68d9df35b374819690b63c6dca25cce602e7edb03d694e44", "content": [{"annotations": [], "text": "Yes, your patient can receive funding for a CPAP machine through the Assistive Devices Program (ADP) in Ontario. Here are the details:\n\n### **Funding Information:**\n- **ADP Coverage:** 75% of the cost of the CPAP machine.\n- **Patient Share:** The patient is responsible for the remaining 25% of the cost.\n- **Low-Income Assistance:** Patients with low income may be eligible for the Chronic Equipment Pool (CEP), which can eliminate their 25% share.\n\n### **Eligibility Requirements:**\n- A valid prescription from an authorized prescriber is required for funding approval.\n- The patient must have a diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea syndrome (OSAS).\n\n### **Additional Information:**\n- **Repair Coverage:** Not covered by ADP.\n  \n### **Resources:**\nFor more detailed information and guidelines, you can refer to the following official ADP documents:\n- [ADP Respiratory Equipment Manual](https://files.ontario.ca/moh-adp-policy-and-administration-manual-respiratory-equipment-2024-11-08.pdf)\n- [ADP Core Policies and Procedures Manual](https://files.ontario.ca/moh-adp-policies-and-procedures-manual-assistive-devices-program-2023-07-01.pdf)\n\n### **Next Steps:**\n1. Obtain a valid prescription for the CPAP machine.\n2. Submit the application for ADP funding to get the coverage started.\n\nMake sure to verify this information for any updates or changes in policy.", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message"}','2025-09-29 01:22:04');
INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(73,'8762a967-4491-4ba9-96d2-67d35acc7560','{"content": "What are the generic alternatives to Januvia?", "role": "user"}','2025-09-29 01:22:23');
