IABETIC AGENTS ORAL ANTI-DIABETIC AGENTS\\\\nPrice: $1.7785 per unit\\\\nDaily Cost: $N/A\\\\nCoverage: General Benefit\\\\nSection 3\\\\nChronic Use\\\\n\\\\nManufacturer: MEK\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\",\"annotations\":null,\"meta\":null}", "type": "function_call_output"}','2025-09-29 01:24:01');
INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(80,'312e5d7e-1a4e-4e72-b8f5-8a21d4d72255','{"id": "msg_68d9dfb23bb081979615f90e7a2cfc990d08e4346d0b8a5b", "content": [{"annotations": [], "text": "**SUMMARY**: Januvia (Sitagliptin) is currently covered under the Ontario Drug Benefit (ODB). As of now, there are no generic alternatives available for Januvia, although there are specific combination products such as Janumet that include Sitagliptin.\n\n**DETAILED RESPONSE**:\n\n- **Direct Answer**: Januvia, which contains the active ingredient Sitagliptin, does not have a generic alternative currently available in Ontario. \n- **Coverage Details**: Januvia is fully covered under the ODB with multiple strengths available (25mg, 50mg, and 100mg). There are no Limited Use (LU) criteria for this medication, allowing for accessible coverage for eligible patients.\n- **Billing Information**: \n  - **DINs**: \n    - Sitagliptin 25mg: [DIN 02388839]\n    - Sitagliptin 50mg: [DIN 02388847]\n    - Sitagliptin 100mg: [DIN 02303922]\n  - The price for Sitagliptin is approximately $3.2787 per unit.\n- **Substitution Options**: No registered generic alternatives exist specifically for Sitagliptin, but combination products like Janumet (Sitagliptin and Metformin) are available and also covered:\n  - **Janumet**:\n    - DIN 02333864: Sitagliptin 50mg & Metformin 850mg\n    - DIN 02333872: Sitagliptin 50mg & Metformin 1000mg\n- **Alternatives**: While Sitagliptin itself is not generically available, physicians may consider prescribing Janumet if appropriate for the patient''s condition.\n- **Next Steps**: Patients should consult their healthcare providers for a prescription; no prior authorization is needed for Januvia under the ODB.\n\nFor detailed formulary information, refer to the Ontario Drug Benefit Formulary: [ODB Sourcing](https://www.formulary.health.gov.on.ca/formulary/results.xhtml?q=02388839).", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message"}','2025-09-29 01:24:10');
