\nPrice: $0.1811 per unit\\\\nDaily Cost: $N/A\\\\nCoverage: General Benefit\\\\nSection 3 Section 12\\\\nChronic Use\\\\n\\\\nManufacturer: AUR\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\",\"annotations\":null,\"meta\":null}", "type": "function_call_output"}','2025-09-29 01:24:47');
INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(84,'b5d04fed-a19f-47d8-92fc-c77bad49c24e','{"id": "msg_68d9dfe039c08193bcc69d6d70df6b570ce62e83d114d586", "content": [{"annotations": [], "text": "**SUMMARY:** Ozempic (SEMAGLUTIDE) is covered by the Ontario Drug Benefit (ODB) for its authorized indications but is not specifically covered for weight loss. It may be prescribed for type 2 diabetes management.\n\n**DETAILED RESPONSE:**\n\n- **Direct Answer:** Ozempic (DIN: 02540258) is **covered by ODB**; however, it is primarily indicated for the management of type 2 diabetes rather than for weight loss specifically.\n  \n- **Coverage Details:** There are no specific limitations for weight loss; however, utilization must align with its approved therapeutic indications, mainly for diabetes control. As of now, the ODB does not recognize weight loss as an authorized use for this medication under its coverage guidelines.\n\n- **Billing Information:** The cost of Ozempic is approximately $223.26 per unit. It falls under the category of anti-diabetic agents, and no Limited Use codes are associated for weight loss. \n\n- **Substitution Options:** While Ozempic is covered, alternatives include other medications within the diabetes drug class, but they''re subject to similar approval criteria focused on diabetes treatment, not weight management.\n\n- **Alternatives:** If a patient is specifically looking for medication for weight management, over-the-counter options or other prescribed weight-loss medications (not necessarily part of the ODB) may be recommended, but these will not be covered by ODB as well.\n\n- **Next Steps:** For patients with diabetes needing Ozempic, ensure that the prescription aligns with the clinical criteria for diabetes management. Discuss alternative weight loss strategies that do not rely on ODB coverage.\n\nFor further details and guidelines, you can refer to the Ontario Drug Benefit Formulary [here](https://www.formulary.health.gov.on.ca/formulary/results.xhtml?q=02540258).", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message"}','2025-09-29 01:24:54');
